The same promise, made twice
Two columns of equal size. On the left, the promise as a policy: a dashed panel
saying only the treating clinician reads a record and only for care, written
down, trained, audited once a year, and set aside on a bad Tuesday. On the
right, the same promise as a property: a sealed panel saying a read is a step
of a process and a step names what it may reach, so there is no general read
behind it, nothing to set aside, and the attempt is itself the audit entry.
